we have worked on an autonomous mobile manipulator, with the sole goal of collecting waste and disposing it.
equipped with mecanum wheels to smoothly traverse in an industrial environment and a 3 DOF four arm-linkage robot arm to pick up the waste.
uses a oak 3d depth camera, a rp lidar c1 for SLAM, and the rasberry pi 5 as the processor.
uses a 14.8 V 5500 mah, with pull runtime of above 3 hours, we pull 1.5 A on an avg and 2 A peak.  
The max load our robot arm can take is approx 1 kg.
We have a buck converter to step down voltage form 14.8 to 5v for the electronic components.
The ESP32 S3 is equipped with microros and controls the mecanum wheels, it publishes the encoder values to /hazmat/encoder_vel and subscribes to /hazmat/cmd_vel and moves according to what is published there.
The rasberry pi 5 connects to the esp32s3, lidar, oak and the servo driver.


